Why shouldn't the shopkeeper untrap and retrap the box? Who do you think 
puts the traps on boxes to begin with?

Unlocking/locking is easy as shopkeepers all have keys. For consistency 
though, the program should stop shopkeepers giving you a price if you've 
stolen their key[*], or if its a cursed BoH.

[*] Unless they have a wand of opening, and then it should remain 
unlocked.[**]

[**] Unless the obvious...

The whole thing seems like a lot of work. You would have to sell the 
unknown chest and then buy it back at great expense to find out it 
contains. Simply dropping an unknown box gives you a total price (the 
shopkeeper obviously looked inside), but doesn't give you a detailed 
inventory.

